{"path":"std/sync/mpmc/index.html","title":"Module mpmc","description":"Multi-producer, multi-consumer FIFO queue communication primitives.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Module mpmc"}]},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/sync/mpmc/mod.rs.html#1-1444","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"text","value":" 🔬This is a nightly-only experimental API. ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"mpmc_channel"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/126840","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"#126840"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-producer, multi-consumer FIFO queue communication primitives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module provides message-based communication over channels, concretely defined by two types:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Sender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Sender","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Sender"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Sender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Sender","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Sender"}]},{"type":"text","value":"s are used to send data to a set of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":"s where each item sent is delivered to (at most) one receiver. Both sender and receiver are cloneable (multi-producer) such that many threads can send simultaneously to receivers (multi-consumer)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These channels come in two flavors:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An asynchronous, infinitely buffered channel. The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function will return a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(Sender, Receiver)"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple where all sends will be "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"asynchronous"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (they never block). The channel conceptually has an infinite buffer."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A synchronous, bounded channel. The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.sync_channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::sync_channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sync_channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function will return a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(Sender, Receiver)"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple where the storage for pending messages is a pre-allocated buffer of a fixed size. All sends will be "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"synchronous"}]},{"type":"text","value":" by blocking until there is buffer space available. Note that a bound of 0 is allowed, causing the channel to become a “rendezvous” channel where each sender atomically hands off a message to a receiver."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"disconnection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disconnection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The send and receive operations on channels will all return a "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html","title":"enum std::result::Result","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Result"}]},{"type":"text","value":" indicating whether the operation succeeded or not. An unsuccessful operation is normally indicative of the other half of a channel having “hung up” by being dropped in its corresponding thread."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once half of a channel has been deallocated, most operations can no longer continue to make progress, so "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html#variant.Err","title":"variant std::result::Result::Err","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Err"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will be returned. Many applications will continue to "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html#method.unwrap","title":"method std::result::Result::unwrap","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"unwrap"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the results returned from this module, instigating a propagation of failure among threads if one unexpectedly dies."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simple usage:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"#![feature(mpmc_channel)]\n\nuse std::thread;\nuse std::sync::mpmc::channel;\n\n// Create a simple streaming channel\nlet (tx, rx) = channel();\nthread::spawn(move || {\n    tx.send(10).unwrap();\n});\nassert_eq!(rx.recv().unwrap(), 10);"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0A%23!%5Bfeature(mpmc_channel)%5D%0A%0A%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++use+std::sync::mpmc::channel;%0A++++%0A++++//+Create+a+simple+streaming+channel%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+channel();%0A++++thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++tx.send(10).unwrap();%0A++++%7D);%0A++++assert_eq!(rx.recv().unwrap(),+10);%0A%7D&version=nightly&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared usage:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"#![feature(mpmc_channel)]\n\nuse std::thread;\nuse std::sync::mpmc::channel;\n\nthread::scope(|s| {\n    // Create a shared channel that can be sent along from many threads\n    // where tx is the sending half (tx for transmission), and rx is the receiving\n    // half (rx for receiving).\n    let (tx, rx) = channel();\n    for i in 0..10 {\n        let tx = tx.clone();\n        s.spawn(move || {\n            tx.send(i).unwrap();\n        });\n    }\n\n    for _ in 0..5 {\n        let rx1 = rx.clone();\n        let rx2 = rx.clone();\n        s.spawn(move || {\n            let j = rx1.recv().unwrap();\n            assert!(0 <= j && j < 10);\n        });\n        s.spawn(move || {\n            let j = rx2.recv().unwrap();\n            assert!(0 <= j && j < 10);\n        });\n    }\n})"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0A%23!%5Bfeature(mpmc_channel)%5D%0A%0A%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++use+std::sync::mpmc::channel;%0A++++%0A++++thread::scope(%7Cs%7C+%7B%0A++++++++//+Create+a+shared+channel+that+can+be+sent+along+from+many+threads%0A++++++++//+where+tx+is+the+sending+half+(tx+for+transmission),+and+rx+is+the+receiving%0A++++++++//+half+(rx+for+receiving).%0A++++++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+channel();%0A++++++++for+i+in+0..10+%7B%0A++++++++++++let+tx+=+tx.clone();%0A++++++++++++s.spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++++++++++tx.send(i).unwrap();%0A++++++++++++%7D);%0A++++++++%7D%0A++++%0A++++++++for+_+in+0..5+%7B%0A++++++++++++let+rx1+=+rx.clone();%0A++++++++++++let+rx2+=+rx.clone();%0A++++++++++++s.spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++++++++++let+j+=+rx1.recv().unwrap();%0A++++++++++++++++assert!(0+%3C=+j+%26%26+j+%3C+10);%0A++++++++++++%7D);%0A++++++++++++s.spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++++++++++let+j+=+rx2.recv().unwrap();%0A++++++++++++++++assert!(0+%3C=+j+%26%26+j+%3C+10);%0A++++++++++++%7D);%0A++++++++%7D%0A++++%7D)%0A%7D&version=nightly&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Propagating panics:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"#![feature(mpmc_channel)]\n\nuse std::sync::mpmc::channel;\n\n// The call to recv() will return an error because the channel has already\n// hung up (or been deallocated)\nlet (tx, rx) = channel::<i32>();\ndrop(tx);\nassert!(rx.recv().is_err());"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0A%23!%5Bfeature(mpmc_channel)%5D%0A%0A%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::sync::mpmc::channel;%0A++++%0A++++//+The+call+to+recv()+will+return+an+error+because+the+channel+has+already%0A++++//+hung+up+(or+been+deallocated)%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+channel::%3Ci32%3E();%0A++++drop(tx);%0A++++assert!(rx.recv().is_err());%0A%7D&version=nightly&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"reexports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-exports"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"reexport.RecvError","term":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"pub use crate::sync::mpsc::RecvError;"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reexport.RecvTimeoutError","term":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"pub use crate::sync::mpsc::RecvTimeoutError;"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reexport.SendError","term":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"pub use crate::sync::mpsc::SendError;"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reexport.TryRecvError","term":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"pub use crate::sync::mpsc::TryRecvError;"}],"definition":[]},{"id":"reexport.TrySendError","term":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"pub use crate::sync::mpsc::TrySendError;"}],"definition":[]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"structs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structs"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.IntoIter.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::IntoIter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"IntoIter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An owning iterator over messages on a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":", created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html#method.into_iter","title":"method std::sync::mpmc::Receiver::into_iter","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"into_iter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Iter.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Iter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An iterator over messages on a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":", created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html#method.iter","title":"method std::sync::mpmc::Receiver::iter","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"iter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"The receiving half of Rust’s "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.sync_channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::sync_channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sync_channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":") type. Different threads can share this "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" by cloning it."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Sender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Sender","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sender"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"The sending-half of Rust’s synchronous "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.TryIter.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::TryIter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TryIter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An iterator that attempts to yield all pending values for a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpmc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":", created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Receiver.html#method.try_iter","title":"method std::sync::mpmc::Receiver::try_iter","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"try_iter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"enums","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enums"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/enum.SendTimeoutError.html","title":"enum std::sync::mpmc::SendTimeoutError","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SendTimeoutError"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An error returned from the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/struct.Sender.html#method.send_timeout","title":"method std::sync::mpmc::Sender::send_timeout","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"send_timeout"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Functions"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::channel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a new asynchronous channel, returning the sender/receiver halves."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpmc/fn.sync_channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpmc::sync_channel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sync_channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a new synchronous, bounded channel."}]}]}]}}
